# Shabakat — What To Use

Windows-only .NET MAUI Blazor Hybrid app. Prefer these tools and stay within this stack.

## Technologies

- **App**: .NET 10 MAUI Blazor Hybrid (`Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor`, `UseMaui`)
- **Target**: `net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0` only — do not add Android/iOS/MacCatalyst
- **UI**: Blazor components under `Components/` (`.razor`), not native MAUI pages for screens
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 only — see CSS files below
- **Dev tooling**: `Microsoft.Maui.DevFlow.Agent` + `Microsoft.Maui.DevFlow.Blazor` (DEBUG)
- **Layers**: put logic in `Domain/`, `Application/`, `Infrastructure/` — keep UI thin

### CSS (exactly two files)

| Role | Path |
|------|------|
| Input (edit this) | `Styles/app.css` |
| Output (built; do not hand-edit) | `wwwroot/app.css` |

Build with `npm run tw:build` or `npm run tw:watch`.

- **Do not** add `.razor.css` / scoped CSS — it is buggy in this MAUI Blazor Hybrid setup
- **Do not** add extra CSS files; put all styles in `Styles/app.css`

```csharp
// ✅ Windows-only TFM in Shabakat.csproj
<TargetFramework>net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0</TargetFramework>

// ❌ Do not restore multi-target
// <TargetFrameworks>net10.0-android;net10.0-ios;...</TargetFrameworks>
```

## MCP

- **`user-maui-devflow`**: run/inspect the live MAUI app (tree, tap, screenshot, navigate, logs, network). Prefer this over guessing UI state.
- **`ctx7` / find-docs skill**: fetch current docs for MAUI, Blazor, Tailwind, or NuGet APIs before answering from memory.
- Do **not** use Flutter/Dart MCP or browser automation for this desktop MAUI app unless the user explicitly asks.

## Skills

Prefer these **project skills** under `.cursor/skills/` (read and follow the matching `SKILL.md` before coding):

| Need | Skill |
|------|--------|
| MAUI Blazor Hybrid setup, BlazorWebView, platform/DI/navigation with MAUI | `maui-blazor-development` |
| Blazor components, lifecycle, state, routing, forms, auth, JS interop, perf | `blazor-expert` |
| Build/run/inspect/debug loop, DevFlow, UI tree, screenshots, CDP WebView | `maui-ai-debugging` |

Also use when relevant (global/user skills):

| Need | Skill |
|------|--------|
| Library/API/docs (MAUI, Blazor, Tailwind, NuGet) | `find-docs` (ctx7) |
| UI polish / layout / a11y review | `ui-ux-pro-max` or `web-design-guidelines` |

For live app inspection, combine `maui-ai-debugging` with MCP `user-maui-devflow`. This project is **Windows-only** — ignore iOS/Android/Mac/Linux paths in those skills unless the user asks.

## Do not introduce

React/Next, Flutter, Electron, CSS frameworks other than Tailwind v4, Blazor scoped CSS (`.razor.css`), extra CSS files, or extra mobile targets unless the user explicitly requests them.
